{"text": " If a shirt costs 1,000 rupees and you get a 20% discount, how much do you actually save? Percentage simply means per 100. It tells us how much something represents out of 100. Here is the key formula, percentage equals part divided by total times 100. For example, 20 students out of 50 passed, which is 40%. To calculate faster, remember these shortcuts, 10% divide by 10. 5% half of 10. 1% divide by 100. For 15% of 200, 10% is 20, 5% is 10, getting 30. Here is the golden aptitude trick, x% of y is equal to y% of x. 25% of 80 is the same as 80% of 25. Both equal 20. Remember, per 100, part over total times 100, and use mental shortcuts. Practice these and master percentages. Learn smart, solve faster.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.18, "text": " If a shirt costs 1,000 rupees and you get a 20% discount, how much do you actually save?", "tokens": [50364, 759, 257, 8336, 5497, 502, 11, 1360, 24638, 293, 291, 483, 257, 945, 4, 11635, 11, 577, 709, 360, 291, 767, 3155, 30, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16606112607975596, "compression_ratio": 1.516260162601626, "no_speech_prob": 0.012693346478044987, "words": [{"word": " If", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.32, "probability": 0.8375988602638245}, {"word": " a", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.56, "probability": 0.9903723001480103}, {"word": " shirt", "start": 0.56, "end": 0.72, "probability": 0.518310010433197}, {"word": " costs", "start": 0.72, "end": 1.04, "probability": 0.9866805672645569}, {"word": " 1", "start": 1.04, "end": 1.3, "probability": 0.38332098722457886}, {"word": ",000", "start": 1.3, "end": 1.66, "probability": 0.927476167678833}, {"word": " rupees", "start": 1.66, "end": 2.08, "probability": 0.7644378542900085}, {"word": " and", "start": 2.08, "end": 2.28, "probability": 0.8595812916755676}, {"word": " you", "start": 2.28, "end": 2.36, "probability": 0.9971133470535278}, {"word": " get", "start": 2.36, "end": 2.5, "probability": 0.9971516728401184}, {"word": " a", "st